    {
      "case": "a-past-tense-paraphrase-passes-the-schema",
      "valid": true,
      "schemaCannotCatch": "AE3's identity rule - that the action string IS the permission string. 'invoice.voided' matches the pattern and is a well-formed event; what is wrong with it is that the product declares the permission 'invoice.void', and a second vocabulary has just started. This is the drift the ledger's AE3 static check exists for: read the declared permission set, assert every emitted action is one of them or a reserved auth.* action. Recorded here as a passing case so the file does not imply the schema catches it.",
      "event": {
        "schema_version": 1,
        "event_id": "01923e8a-7f4e-7cc3-9a2b-3f8d2c1b0b07",
